# No build tooling lives on this branch yet — the scaffold arrives with #3 and
# brings a fuller list. This minimal file exists so that a local build or an
# `npm install` run against this branch cannot be swept into a commit by a
# `git add -A`. Without it there is nothing at all stopping that, and the
# failure is quiet: thousands of files, staged and committed, in a PR whose
# diff nobody scrolls to the bottom of.
node_modules/
dist/
_site/

# Claude Code agent worktrees: full checkouts of this repo nested inside it.
.claude/
